      "id": 1,
      "claim": "A plant stem’s primary functions are structural support and transport of water, minerals, and photosynthates between roots and aerial parts.",
      "evidence": "Botany textbooks (e.g., Raven et al., *Biology of Plants*) describe stems as the main axis that holds leaves/flowers upright and contains xylem and phloem for upward water flow and downward sugar transport.",
      "weight": 0.25,
      "depends_on": []
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "claim": "An elevator system consists of a vertical shaft that is a load‑bearing structural element and a car that moves goods or people between floors.",
      "evidence": "Engineering references on elevator design state that the shaft provides the building’s vertical support while the elevator car provides vertical transport of loads.",
      "weight": 0.15,
      "depends_on": []
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "claim": "The elevator shaft supplies structural support to the building, analogous to the stem’s support role in a plant.",
      "evidence": "The shaft is designed to bear vertical loads and resist lateral forces, functioning as the building’s backbone.",
      "weight": 0.15,
      "depends_on": [2]
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "claim": "The elevator car transports supplies between floors, analogous to the stem’s transport of water, minerals, and sugars between roots and shoots.",
      "evidence": "Elevators move materials vertically, mirroring the vertical movement of fluids in a plant’s vascular system.",
      "weight": 0.15,
      "depends_on": [2]
    },
    {
      "id": 5,
      "claim": "Option D (an elevator transporting supplies from one floor to another) incorporates both transport and support functions, matching the dual role of a plant stem better than the other options.",
      "evidence": "Combining steps 1, 3, and 4 shows that D provides an analogue for both major stem functions, whereas the alternatives lack one or both.",
      "weight": 0.20,
      "depends_on": [1, 3, 4]
    },
    {
      "id": 6,
      "claim": "Option A (an anchor) provides only static support and no transport, so it matches only part of the stem’s role.",
      "evidence": "An anchor holds a boat in place but does not convey materials between parts, unlike a stem.",
      "weight": 0.05,
      "depends_on": [1]
    },
    {
      "id": 7,
      "claim": "Options B (snack company) and C (colorful sign) are unrelated to either structural support or transport functions of a stem.",
      "evidence": "These options describe food production and visual attraction, which have no correspondence to stem physiology.",
      "weight": 0.05,
      "depends_on": [1]
    }
  ],
  "answer": "D",
  "confidence": 0.97,
